 "limitation": "A high share says the reading is concentrated in one country; it does not say that country likes the star more, because the four editions serve different numbers of readers and different reading habits, and the per-million scaling only removes the first of those. Reads count people opening an encyclopaedia article, which is not fandom and not sales. And the floor and the four-edition rule are ours, so a different cut would move which names appear.",
